# Cursor Rules — Mandatory Architecture Specification

Read and follow `AGENTS.md` and `agent-kit/platform/rules-manifest.yaml` unconditionally.

- Run `bash agent-kit/scripts/run-rules-manifest.sh --changed` before completing any code change.
- Never violate vertical slice folder structure.
- Never use `any` in TypeScript, `!!` in Kotlin, or naked type assertions / panics in Go.
- Never use `for`/`while` loops inside features/domain/components — use functional combinators.
- Never omit tenant context on queries or mutate without an `Idempotency-Key`.
- Preserve §14 Identifier Taxonomy across all handlers and HTTP calls without aliasing.
